  "title": "CVE-2026-30950 Allows Chat Session Hijacking In AutoGPT",
  "summary": "ZeroPath Research discovered an authenticated IDOR in AutoGPT (CVE-2026-30950) that lets any logged-in user hijack any other user's chat session with a single PATCH request, exposing the full conversation history and locking out the original owner. Affects autogpt-platform-backend >= 0.6.36, < 0.6.51; patched in 0.6.51.",
